  "id": "calendar-override-expansion",
  "instruction": "Repair service.solve(q). This self-contained calendar uses integer civil minutes, not external timezone rules. Generate count nominal occurrences (id i, local time start+i*step), with step>0 and count<=16. IDs always refer to this original counted sequence. Cancel removes IDs; cancellation wins over replacement. replace maps decimal ID strings to new local times; out-of-range IDs are ignored. Apply cancellation/replacement before filtering. zones is an ordered contiguous partition of UTC integer minutes [lo,hi), each with an integer offset; civil=UTC+offset. If multiple UTC values represent a local minute choose the earliest. For a nonexistent civil minute, choose the first forward-offset transition in UTC interval order whose civil gap contains it, shift forward by that gap width, and resolve the shifted civil minute again. Repeat until a supported UTC representation is found; direct representations always take precedence over gaps. If no direct representation or applicable gap exists, raise ValueError, including after a shift. Convert every retained event, then include it iff UTC is in the half-open window; return [{id,utc}], sorted by UTC then ID. Converting a retained unsupported time raises even if the window would exclude it. No source argument may change. UTC zone range is within[-500,500], at most4 intervals; all other input shapes are valid.\nAll input domains and required behavior are stated above. Preserve all arguments. Use Python standard library only, no package installation or network. The supplied verify.py is a frozen smoke check, not the complete contract. The controller reporting contract specifies phase-bound observations; never substitute an observation from another phase or invent an execution.\n\nAllowed content edits: service.py, recurrence.py, zones.py, overrides.py. Change only the contents of those existing regular files. Preserve their modes. All other initial files, directories, modes, and Git metadata are frozen; incidental stat-cache refresh is handled by the common controller contract. Do not create, remove or rename workspace files. Put temporary probes under /tmp.\n",
